# What NOT to upload to Cloud Build. This file exists specifically to break
# gcloud's default behaviour: with no .gcloudignore, gcloud derives one from
# .gitignore, which would exclude watchlist.js — the deploy would succeed and
# the container would die at startup with "watchlist.js not found".
#
# So: gitignored means "not in the public repo", NOT "absent from production".
# The watchlist is uploaded from the deploying machine and baked into the
# image. Deploys must therefore run somewhere that has a real watchlist.js.

.git
.gitignore
node_modules
.env
.env.*
*.db
*.sqlite
.DS_Store
.neon
claims-snapshot-*.json
.claude
